+------------- MULTI‑SENSOR FIRE‑PREVENTION MATRIX -------------+

  SENSORS:
    NODE_I    (current sense via RSENSE)
    NODE_TH   (hotspot NTC)
    NODE_CASE (enclosure NTC)
    NODE_AIR  (airflow sensor, e.g., thermistor or vane switch)

  COMPARATORS:
    U_I   : NODE_I   vs I_REF_MAX   → I_FAULT
    U_TH  : NODE_TH  vs T_REF_HOT   → TH_FAULT
    U_CASE: NODE_CASE vs T_REF_CASE → CASE_FAULT
    U_AIR : NODE_AIR vs AIR_MIN     → AIR_FAULT

  LOGIC OR:
    I_FAULT ----\
                 +----> FIRE_FAULT_LINE
    TH_FAULT ---/
    CASE_FAULT -\
                 +----> FIRE_FAULT_LINE
    AIR_FAULT --/

  FIRE_FAULT_LINE --> [Q_MASTER] NPN
                        |
                        +--> DISABLE_DRIVER
                        +--> LED_FIRE_FAULT

  BEHAVIOR:
  - Any single sensor crossing its limit asserts FIRE_FAULT_LINE.
  - Driver is immediately disabled and fault indicated.
  - You can weight sensors (e.g., require TH_FAULT + CASE_FAULT) by adding AND gates.
